comments[91]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T16:46:19.458Z",codex-astra,"Main 1a8ce23 still binds item reads to owner/slug and caches PmClient by tracker path. Full issue and main history inspected. The pinned SDK 2026.11.2 PmClientOptions exports only pmRoot, cwd, author and noExtensions; no native-backend binding. Open upstream backend contracts remain tracked by pm-cli #1399, #1587 and #1588. Implement the authorized observational item-read boundary with live grant checks, scoped client identity, certified complete reads and safe refusals. Preserve existing filesystem and no-git behavior; split native provider, mutations and durable events into acceptance-driven Features. Refs #260; no native database support claim."
  "2026-11-06T16:50:45.530Z",codex-astra,"Failing-first proof on main 1a8ce23: authorized-project-reads.test.ts fails all six route cases (7 tests including parent). A real SDK marker extension activates on viewer get/search/board/export/calendar reads; historical reads lack no-store. Real PostgreSQL grants and a no-git SDK tracker are used. The production slice replaces these six routes with a narrow observational SDK reader, cache identity scoped to project/principal/effective grant/storage binding, and live checks before queued work and immediately before releasing data."
  "2026-11-06T16:57:23.143Z",codex-astra,"Follow-up Features with explicit acceptance criteria: pm-web-native-provider (native binding, remaining reads and graph ProjectionSource), pm-web-native-mutations (SDK writes, settings, decisions and durable idempotency), pm-web-native-events (native history, durable scoped events and resume cursors). The current slice covers get, at, search, board, export and calendar. Existing graph, paginated list, history panels and resume contracts remain separate. Documentation states the native-provider gap and authorization linearization boundary without claiming a cross-store snapshot."
  "2026-11-06T17:00:36.421Z",codex-astra,"Behavioral revert proofs in a disposable package worktree: restore only main route handlers -> 8/8 selected tests fail (extension activation, missing no-store and unsafe unavailable semantics); remove only the final authorize call -> 4/4 in-flight tests fail with missing expected rejection; remove principal from the cache key -> 1/1 fails equal-permission principal isolation; remove permission from binding identity -> 1/1 fails changed-grant binding isolation. All failures are intended assertions, zero cancellations or skips. Fixed functions restored in finally; passing restored tests follow. SDK version is unchanged. GitHub issue read also succeeded via gh issue view with explicit JSON fields after the classic-project query failed."
  "2026-11-06T17:03:20.619Z",codex-astra,An additional failing-first queue regression found relative PROJECTS_ROOT paths and resolved SDK paths could bypass the shared local workspace queue. The real-process test fails with resolved read binding overtook the existing relative-root queue. Normalize both queue identities with path.resolve inside runSerialized. This preserves the promised local mutation/read ordering for both supported path forms; independent OS writers remain outside the in-process queue.
  "2026-11-06T17:07:21.600Z",codex-astra,"Final local source verification: linked authorized-project-reads tests pass 14/14 through pm test --run --match test-concurrency=2 --progress (71.8 seconds, no skipped or canceled tests). Broader targeted command: 56/57 pass; the unchanged spawn fallback 120ms overlap assertion observed independent process startup after the first process ended. Its isolated exact test rerun passes 1/1; existing timing investigation pm-web-qdhx remains relevant. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test and npm run lint pass. Clean source-identical verification copy passes npm run docstring (205 files, 938 declarations) and npm run duplication (350 sources, zero clones, unchanged zero threshold). Build output regenerated. CI owns full npm/Bun release gates per task. Existing history remains a byte-identical prefix extension of main. Five failing behavioral proofs are recorded above; fixed implementations restored. Releasing own claim for PR review; roadmap and Features remain open."
  "2026-11-06T17:16:40.139Z",codex-astra,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/305 is open with Refs #260. Implementation commit f698a773b2a5b06f498c854015ae6e29f1b618dc is pushed; commit identity and staged privacy checks pass. Initial CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/42258944134 and CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/42258944041 are queued, not verified. CodeRabbit manual review is queued through the required shared queue; automatic review was skipped, and Greptile/Sourcery notices do not constitute approval. Initial state has zero unresolved threads and zero unvoted bot comments. This receipt is recorded before final-head CI verification. No merge, release, hosted operation or sibling-branch change was performed."
