  "2026-11-06T17:39:45.552Z",codex-astra,"Cutoff handoff for PR #305: current code/test head 537c47cf3494afa8c14ca3a2cd2000a5194cc48a has passing CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/42260986109. Full CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/42260986117 still has Node 22 and Node 26 queued at the shared rules 30-minute cutoff. No full gate success is claimed. CodeQL thread PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c60nWDm was fixed in 537c47c, replied to and resolved; marker regression 7/7 passes. CodeRabbit remains in the shared manual queue with zero completed reviews on this head and no finished or NOT REVIEWED receipt; quota and skip notices are not approval. Latest state: zero unresolved threads, zero unvoted recognized bot comments, no reviewer issue references. Final evidence-only commit follows this receipt and requires fresh CI; its pending run will be linked in the PR and final handoff. Temporary test database is stopped; all local tests are finished. All four touched items remain unclosed and this authors claim is released. Remaining risks: native-provider roadmap Features, pending full CI/manual review, and the documented existing overlap timing case. No additional pm CLI defect was found; the native handle gap is the already-tracked upstream contract dependency."
  "2026-11-06T21:11:12.958Z",codex-astra,"Resumed PR #305 at pushed head 850b7c3. Worktree is clean and git pull --ff-only is current. Node 22 CI passed; Node 26 failed its full npm release gate. CodeRabbit completed the head review with three unresolved threads plus one test nitpick. Investigating exact CI failure and addressing package documentation, safe correlated diagnostics and queued-read revocation coverage. No completed implementation or revert proofs are being redone. All original scope and privacy boundaries remain in force."
  "2026-11-06T21:15:58.355Z",codex-astra,"CI root cause: Node 26 ran 898 tests, 897 passed; only the partial-age-index EXPLAIN assertion failed because a tiny shared table allowed the legacy created_at index to tie the desired settled_at index. The test now shadows the real table in its session with a temporary LIKE table, clones every production index, seeds 10000 synthetic pending/settled rows, and ANALYZEs only that table. Existing required-index, age-condition and no-sequential-scan assertions remain unchanged. Negative controls drop each required index only in pg_temp and verify the same assertions fail. The focused plan test passes 1/1 including both negative controls. No runtime SQL or thresholds changed. CodeRabbit findings are being addressed; POST search remains explicitly tracked in native-provider acceptance criteria."
  "2026-11-06T21:20:10.891Z",codex-astra,"Review fixes verified: tracker-linked authorized-read tests pass 16/16; tracker-linked PostgreSQL tests pass 3/3, including the real sweep plans and missing-index negative controls. npm run typecheck:server and npm run build:test pass; lint, duplication and docstring gates pass in the matching clean verification copy (350 sources, zero clones; 205 files, 938 declarations). Safe diagnostics preserve only allowlisted SDK categories and the existing generated request id, with unchanged generic 503 responses. The diagnostic regression failed first with no records, and reverting only projectItemRead to the prior helper fails 1/1. Removing only pre-read authorize fails the new queued-revocation assertion even though final authorization still rejects; restored tests pass 2/2. Package docs now use repository blob URLs and explicitly limit the guarantee to GET search. POST search authorization remains tracked in native-provider acceptance criteria."
  "2026-11-06T21:23:06.948Z",codex-astra,"Ready for the next review round: all three CodeRabbit threads are addressed, and its queued-revocation nitpick now schedules a real SDK get callback after initial authorization. Removing only the pre-read check makes that callback run and fails 1/1; restoring it plus the diagnostic handler passes 2/2. The final PostgreSQL fixture preserves valid outcome states and timestamps; tracker-linked checks pass 3/3 with both intended-index negative controls. Final lint, test typecheck, zero-duplication and docstring gates pass against the matching restored verification copy. Source build output is regenerated. Documentation-only fixes require no artificial runtime tests. Releasing this authors claim; after this final tracker write the changelog will be regenerated and checked, then the code/tracker commit pushed and all review threads answered in one batch. Full CI and manual re-review will be checked on that pushed head, subject to the explicit 23:30Z hard stop."
